        <mxCell id="l42" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align:left;line-height:1.5;font-size:12px;color:#5A6B7B&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why a discrete command name on the wire, not a raw Twist?&lt;/b&gt; &lt;code&gt;{&quot;command&quot;:&quot;forward&quot;}&lt;/code&gt; keeps the MQTT contract stable no matter how the velocity mapping evolves. Turning &quot;forward&quot; into 0.20 m/s is explicitly the agent&#39;s job — &lt;code&gt;dispatcher.py&lt;/code&gt;, one small function, one place to change.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="66" y="950" width="1600" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
